---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Prose
  title="Returns and cancellations"
  standfirst="You have 14 days to change your mind, and separate rights if something is faulty."
  updated="TBD"
>
  <h2>Your right to cancel</h2>
  <p>
    You can cancel your order for any reason within 14 days of the day you
    receive it. You do not have to give a reason.
  </p>
  <p>
    Items here are printed after you order, but they are printed from my own
    standard designs — so I treat them as ordinary goods and give you the full
    cancellation right rather than relying on the exemption for bespoke or
    personalised items.
  </p>

  <h2>How to cancel</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with your order
    number and tell me you are cancelling. A clear statement is enough — there
    is no form to fill in.
  </p>
  <p>
    Then send the item back within 14 days of telling me. Return postage is
    yours to pay unless the item is faulty or not what you ordered.
  </p>

  <h2>Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    I refund within 14 days of the item coming back to me — or of you showing
    me it has been sent, whichever is sooner. The refund covers what you paid
    for the item plus the standard outbound delivery charge.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you have handled the item more than you would in a shop and reduced its
    value, I may reduce the refund to reflect that.
  </p>

  <h2>Faulty or wrong items</h2>
  <p>
    If something arrives faulty, damaged, or not as described, you have separate
    rights under the Consumer Rights Act 2015 that sit on top of the 14-day
    cancellation right. Tell me within 30 days and you can have a full refund.
    After that, a repair or replacement.
  </p>
  <p>Return postage on faulty items is on me.</p>

  <h2>Made-to-measure and custom work</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing currently sold here is custom. If I ever sell something made to your
    own specification — a bespoke size, an engraved name, or a model generated
    to your input — the 14-day cancellation right does not apply to it, and I
    will say so clearly on that product's page before you buy.
  </p>
</Prose>
